./.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-21bsr2_compiled-build-interop/TASK-260720-1673lr_curator-shared-build-suite-consumer/README.md:10:With CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT set, the Go consumer enumerates every shared compiled-build case exactly once and fails on unknown, missing, duplicate, or skipped case IDs. When the suite-defined result sink is supplied, it emits exactly one schema-valid JSON Lines record per case with the verified suite digest, normalized outcome, compiler boundary, persistent-mutation class, and exact launch argv, stdout, stderr, and exit status; it emits no implementation-owned expected value or release claim. The unmodified shared fixture proves cache miss, verified hit, corrupt or untrusted rebuild, compiler-free and mutation-free dry-run, build-root context and runtime exclusion, failed-build rollback, recovery, currentness, repair, locked GC, two-project isolation, and explicit launch. Every shared negative case is rejected in the expected normalized class and at the required before-build or before-mutation boundary. Test homes, project roots, Go caches, and subprocess recording are isolated per case; no binary hash or local oracle is introduced. Focused external-suite tests and go test ./... pass when the suite is supplied, while developer runs may skip only when CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT and the result sink are both absent.
