./.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_csk-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-2jfnz6_protected-build-cache-posix/README.md:10:The manager creates a private owner-controlled boundary and validates effective-UID ownership, no group or other write access, private directories, regular singly linked receipt and artifact files, link-free containment, derived artifact path, size, hash, canonical receipt bytes, and complete expected input on every lookup and again before publication. An untrusted or corrupt candidate is never adopted even when internally self-consistent; dry-run reports a forced rebuild without mutation; real work builds into new protected state. Publication handles identical concurrent winners by discarding the loser and treats different bytes for one key as corruption or nondeterminism. Entries become immutable in ordinary use while locked GC remains possible. POSIX-focused pytest and strict mypy pass.
./.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-21bsr2_compiled-build-interop/TASK-260720-2g7avf_shared-compiled-build-interop-cases/README.md:7:Work in curator-spec after TASK-260720-1s1vr6 and TASK-260720-cw39jh. Extend the exact Go fixture path landed by TASK-260720-1s1vr6 rather than adding a second fixture. Own conformance/v1/vectors/compiled-build-interop.json, its generator and tests in tools/generate-vectors, conformance/v1/manifest.json inventory, and the suite-owned test-only consumer-result transport and JSON record contract. Define portable install, cache, dry-run, lifecycle, and launch cases by referencing the authoritative build-driver and manager-lifecycle vectors wherever possible. Do not duplicate schema or lifecycle payloads, compare platform-dependent binary bytes, prescribe manager-home paths, import implementation packages, create a user-facing manager API, or update release pins.
